From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lens0021 <lorentz0021@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 07:10:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] winewayland: Give back the size a window had before it was
 maximized

Unmaximizing a window did nothing. The window stayed at the size it had
while maximized, and the compositor kept resending the same configure.

The configure that drops the maximized state carries a size, but a
configure without a state that demands strict size adherence is only a
hint, so the driver throws the size away. What is left is a style bit
flipped by hand, WS_MAXIMIZE cleared with no resize, and nothing that
remembers how big the window used to be.

Win32 remembers. The normal placement is saved when the window is
maximized, and SC_RESTORE puts it back. The minimize case right above
this one already works that way.
---
 dlls/winewayland.drv/window.c | 26 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 26 insertions(+)

diff --git a/dlls/winewayland.drv/window.c b/dlls/winewayland.drv/window.c
--- a/dlls/winewayland.drv/window.c
+++ b/dlls/winewayland.drv/window.c
@@ -600,6 +600,32 @@ static void wayland_configure_window(HWND hwnd)
         return;
     }
 
+    /* The same thing one state down: the compositor has taken the window out
+     * of the maximized state. That configure carries a size, but without a
+     * state that demands strict adherence it is only a hint, and the code
+     * above has already dropped it. Clearing WS_MAXIMIZE by hand, as the code
+     * below does, leaves the window at the size it had while maximized and
+     * nothing is left that remembers how big it used to be. The window never
+     * comes back and the compositor keeps resending the same configure.
+     *
+     * Win32 does remember: the normal placement saved when the window was
+     * maximized. Ack the configure and send SC_RESTORE so that placement is
+     * put back, which starts a fresh configure cycle. */
+    style = NtUserGetWindowLongW(hwnd, GWL_STYLE);
+    if (!(state & (WAYLAND_SURFACE_CONFIG_STATE_MAXIMIZED |
+                   WAYLAND_SURFACE_CONFIG_STATE_FULLSCREEN)) &&
+        (style & WS_MAXIMIZE) && !(style & WS_MINIMIZE))
+    {
+        TRACE("hwnd=%p restoring from maximize\n", hwnd);
+        surface->current = surface->processing;
+        memset(&surface->processing, 0, sizeof(surface->processing));
+        xdg_surface_ack_configure(surface->xdg_surface,
+                                  surface->current.serial);
+        wayland_win_data_release(data);
+        send_message(hwnd, WM_SYSCOMMAND, SC_RESTORE, 0);
+        return;
+    }
+
     SetRect(&rect, 0, 0, width, height);
     rect = map_rect_from_surface(surface, rect);
     OffsetRect(&rect, data->rects.window.left, data->rects.window.top);
